 "annotations": [
  {
   "id": "n-land",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-land",
   "text": "First, because it is the first thing anyone meets — and <b>every row below is one screen at both widths</b>: 1440 light, 360 light, 1440 dark, 360 dark. Built from real components at their real size, fragments rather than whole screens, and on the 1440 board from the WEB app's own components, because a laptop reader must see the tables and the dashboard they will actually get. <b>First launch</b> is the screen an <i>installed</i> app shows: v1 is a PWA (spec §G, <i>the app is installable</i>), and an installed app opens cold — no address bar, no landing page, nothing to have scrolled. It is not a mobile screen; it is what any installed copy shows on a device with no budget on it yet. `LandMotion` draws the pointer states, because a static artboard cannot show motion and the build cannot implement from a description. Two image slots are specified and not filled — `docs/design/image-brief.md` carries the shot list, the licences and the reject list."
  },
  {
   "id": "n-sec",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -250,
   "w": 820,
   "page": "page-sec",
